id: pm-e63v1x
title: Tag-push Release must regenerate the exact-tag changelog before immutable publication
description: "The v2026.9.4 tag-push Release checked the changelog generated before the tag existed, so pm-changelog correctly added the immutable tag date and the release failed before npm publication. Make every exact-tag release source, including ordinary tag pushes, regenerate CHANGELOG.md from the checked-out immutable tag, fail closed on any other dirty path, and preserve normal branch-source drift checks. Recover the existing tag without moving it or creating a second automatic release."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: changelog,exact-tag,release,workflow
created_at: "2026-09-04T13:15:31.270Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-04T13:40:10.152Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-04T13:40:09.610Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-04T13:40:09.610Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-e70zh5
severity: high
environment: GitHub Actions tag-push Release for immutable v2026.9.4
repro_steps: "Checkout v2026.9.4; install/build; run pnpm changelog:pm:check (fails); run pnpm changelog:pm and observe the missing release date is added."
resolution: "Release now regenerates canonical changelog metadata for every exact-tag source under a tracked-path allowlist, while reviewed-main sources retain strict drift checking; tests and documentation cover both paths."
expected_result: "Ordinary tag pushes and recovery dispatches can publish one immutable release without moving the tag, accepting stale changelog content, or allowing unrelated mutations."
actual_result: "Focused contracts, exact full coverage, static/security gates, and a clean temporary v2026.9.4 tag-push acceptance all pass; guarded regeneration produced the dated heading and no product mutation besides CHANGELOG.md."
affected_version: 2026.9.4
component: release-automation
regression: true
customer_impact: "The validated SDK/CLI release cannot reach npm, bunx/npx consumers, or GitHub Release until exact-tag recovery succeeds."
